# Pull requests that moved shipped source and deliberately carry no changelog
# entry. Read by tools/check-changelog-completeness.py.
#
# One per line, `<number>: <reason>`. The reason is required: an exemption
# nobody can audit is how this gate would quietly stop meaning anything, so a
# bare number is an error rather than a skip. Every exemption that applies is
# printed on a passing run too, so what was left out stays visible.
#
1932: comments only; no parser, writer or lint behavior moved.
1933: comments only; benchmark snapshots and corpus counts removed from source.
1960: a performance regression that shipped nowhere. #1916 introduced the iterative Document teardown in this same unreleased window and cost about 11% on a small document; this recovers it. No consumer ever installed the slower form, and #1916's own breaking entry already describes the teardown.
2016: the escape-narrowing probes are windowed rather than rerun. The decisions, the budget spent and the output are unchanged; #1995's entry covers the escape count a reader can see.
2047: canonical-writer state moved behind a scope guard and an interrupted probe restores it. No output moved.
2049: the parser and the lint reader share one typed codepoint line index instead of each building its own. No behavior moved.
2055: a spec corpus pin bump whose engine change is nil; the corpus is a test artifact and nothing shipped moved with it.
2081: abbreviation expansion reuses its text storage. Same output, fewer allocations, and the entry it briefly carried described the allocation rather than anything a consumer sees.
2085: parser source mapping and line buffers moved into their own module. No behavior moved.
2100: the canonical render session owns its pass state instead of a free-standing scope guard. No output moved.
2182: a wall-clock parser guard in the test suite became a counter of the work the parser does. The counter is read by the test; parse output is unchanged.
2210: 0.1.7 - a wall-clock timing guard in the test suite became a counter of the pairings the merge bound refuses. Test-only; no parser or writer output moved.
2244: test-only. The adjacent-definition tests assumed layout accepts a denied reference destination; #2243 made those runs fall back so the loss can carry a span. Every changed line is inside `#[cfg(test)]`.
2247: parser reference definitions, lookup state and the late resolution walk moved into `parse::reference_resolution`, and the streaming scanner asks a lookup function instead of the thread-local map. No behavior moved.
2258: verse whitespace expansion and inline position mapping moved into their own parser modules. No behavior moved.
2265: test-only. Opener-reading counters and their assertions are `#[cfg(test)]`; no parser output moved.
2287: nested-list and colon-group extent scans extracted from list-body rebasing. Same scans in the same order; no behavior moved.
2288: code-fence, comment-fence, line-block and definition-list extent scans extracted from list-body rebasing. No behavior moved.
2292: footnote, quote and table extent scans extracted from list-body rebasing. No behavior moved.
